From 7861d342dfba9cf0f5eef2e7691a1728c5ee781c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:06:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: glyph runs through gfopenfont.library's OF_DrawGlyphsA
 on OpenGPU

GraphicsContextOpenGPU::drawGlyphs no longer hands every run to cairo
(cairo-out item 5, openamigabrowser docs/STEP5-6-WEBCORE.md). The glyph
cache is openfont's, as Dale decided: gfopenfont.library 1.5's
OF_DrawGlyphsA fills each glyph once into its A8 atlas through OpenGPU and
draws every use from it (openamigafont #24).

- OpenGPUGlyphsAmiga.c opens gfopenfont.library itself, version 1 with
  revision 5 or later, with its own base: OpenFontLibrary.c's
  OpenFontBase is left alone. It passes a run to OF_DrawGlyphsA.
  Headers from before revision 5 compile it to "not there".
- OpenGPUPaintAmiga: obgpu_glyphs_here gives where the writer draws now
  (the window or a layer's group, the clip rectangle and the clip's A8
  mask, the transform's linear part), and obgpu_map maps a pen onto it.
- drawGlyphs follows Cairo::drawGlyphs. Each glyph sits at the point plus
  the advances before it, in the fill colour times the global alpha.
  Synthetic bold is drawn twice, the second time moved by its offset. It
  is taken when:
  - the face is an OpenFont face (FontPlatformData::openFontFace) with no
    colour glyphs and no synthetic oblique;
  - the text is filled only, with a colour, source-over, normal blending
    and no shadow;
  - it is anti-aliased, or not anti-aliased with FontSmoothingMode::None
    where OpenGPU takes aliased paths.
  The size on the target is the font's size through the transform. A
  scale to a whole number of pixels uses the cache; any other size, and a
  turned or stretched transform, is a matrix about each pen. The batch
  and cairo's own drawing are sent first, since the library draws at
  once, under OpenFontFace's lock.

Everything else stays cairo's: stroked or shadowed text, gradient or
pattern fills, colour emoji, oblique synthesis and drawGlyphsImmediate.
